# BGMI VPS deploy rule (zero-downtime)

App: PM2 `bgmi`, path `/var/www/bgmi`, port **3001**, site `sensitivitysettings.com`.

## Always use this order

```bash
cd /var/www/bgmi
git fetch && git reset --hard origin/main
npx prisma generate && npx prisma db push
npm run build
# ONLY if build succeeds:
pm2 reload bgmi
curl -sI http://127.0.0.1:3001/ | head -n 3
```

Prefer **`pm2 reload`** over `pm2 restart` so the site does not go fully down.

## Never

- Reload/restart if `npm run build` failed
- Delete `.next` without immediately running a successful `npm run build`
- Run `pm2 kill` during traffic
- Deploy `app/[category]` beside `app/[slug]` (Next.js clash → crash/502). Article route must stay `app/[slug]/[newsSlug]`

## After outage checklist

- Nginx `Connection refused` on `:3001` = Node/PM2 not listening (not always a code bug)
- Check: `grep 'New PM2 Daemon' ~/.pm2/pm2.log | tail -5`
- Ensure: `pm2 startup` + `pm2 save` so PM2 survives reboot
